105 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 78 0 R
/E (1. External CSS: We write the code in a separate file with .css extension and link it to the HTML page using <link>. This is the best way because one file can be linked to many pages.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
106 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 78 0 R
/E (2. Internal CSS: We write the code inside a <style> tag in the <head> of the same page. We use this when we have only one page.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
107 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 78 0 R
/E (3. Inline CSS: We write the style directly inside the HTML tag using the style attribute. It is fast but makes the code messy.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
